WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.3 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Contracts and agreements

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
You will sign agreements before you are fully set up: check each one before you sign.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
A contract is an agreement that creates legal obligations. You will sign some before you are fully set up, so check each one before you sign and keep track of what you have promised.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Check before you sign

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:41.574
Parties and signing: Who the parties are and who may sign; before you register, it may bind you personally. For example: A founder signs the shared-kitchen agreement in her own name before the bakery is registered.

6
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:52.533
Obligations and payment: What each side must do and by when, plus the payment and reporting terms. For example: The supplier delivers flour weekly; the bakery pays within 30 days.

7
00:00:52.533 --> 00:01:03.122
Ownership and liability: Who owns materials and data, confidentiality, liability, insurance and indemnities. For example: The bakery keeps ownership of its training materials when the youth centre uses them.

8
00:01:03.122 --> 00:01:14.911
Ending and law: How the contract ends, and which country’s law applies. For example: The youth centre or the bakery can end the referral agreement with three months’ notice.

9
00:01:15.311 --> 00:01:15.911
Why check every one

10
00:01:15.911 --> 00:01:21.215
1. A signature can make you personally liable before you register.

11
00:01:21.215 --> 00:01:25.778
2. Unclear terms cause disputes with partners you need.

12
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:31.341
3. A register stops you missing dates and obligations.

13
00:01:31.741 --> 00:01:32.341
What you will keep

14
00:01:32.341 --> 00:01:38.385
1. A contracts register from the first agreement, with key dates and obligations.

15
00:01:38.385 --> 00:01:43.689
2. Signed copies stored where all the founders can find them.

16
00:01:43.689 --> 00:01:48.881
3. A pre-signature checklist for every new agreement.

17
00:01:49.281 --> 00:01:49.881
What to avoid

18
00:01:49.881 --> 00:01:54.444
Signing a template without reading or adapting it.

19
00:01:54.444 --> 00:01:59.378
Leaving unclear whether a memorandum of understanding is binding.

20
00:01:59.378 --> 00:02:07.163
Skipping review by someone with a legal background for large, long or unusual contracts.

21
00:02:07.763 --> 00:02:09.563
You set up a contracts register and a pre-signature checklist.

22
00:02:09.563 --> 00:02:13.563
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:15.063 --> 00:02:18.163
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
